  {
    "sha": "d3c9ce44583bb3f98fd3445f5a6caa151724cd0c",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGQzYzljZTQ0NTgzYmIzZjk4ZmQzNDQ1ZjVhNmNhYTE1MTcyNGNkMGM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "mkinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-20T16:23:02Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "mkinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-20T16:23:02Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): judge a reduced-accuracy model at its own chord error, up to 0.02 mm\n\nA model kept at a chord error past DEV_TOL (0.01 mm) had no gouge\ntolerance left once its excess passed 0.01 mm, so every finishing\noperation on it was refused at the post.\n\n- verify::excess_floor: for a chord from DEV_TOL up to the constant\n  WIDE_CHORD_LIMIT (0.02 mm), a law gives back only the promised chord\n  (0.005 mm), not the whole excess. The program verdict is then read at\n  the model's own chord error. Up to DEV_TOL, and past the limit, the\n  #864 law is unchanged.\n- verify::band_growth: collision bands grow by the whole excess, also in\n  the widened range. fidelity_law::band_growth reads it.\n- ProgramId::notes: the engine writes each note through onComment after\n  onOpen. document_program_id fills them from fidelity_note, so each\n  posted program on such a model names the model and the tolerance.\n- The model summary and the MCP note say the same fact.\n- Pins that asserted the old formula for a chord past DEV_TOL are\n  updated to the new rule.\n\nDecision: docs/decisions/2996-wide-verdict.md\n\nFixes #2996\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
